# REQUIRES: verilator
# Constant-shell fold, `--csf-mailbox-builder`: the links from one producer
# class to one reader class whose producer instances are each read by one
# reader instance become lanes of one reader-indexed mailbox (a row per
# reader instance, a lane per link, a masked write at the producer's pass, a
# read of the whole row at the reader's). Driver/Inputs/mailbox: eight Src
# read four a Sink (early and late lanes; Sink's ready fans out and stays a
# link). Each variant exact against its target, channels stalled or not:
# - plain: distributed mailboxes, one of them single-banked (late lanes);
# - blk: block RAM mailboxes (`--link-block-depth 2`, read through the
#   RAM's output register);
# - cp: Src in two copies (a mailbox per producer copy);
# - zl: bubbles, shared write registers and zero-latency links;
# - slr: SLR groups with Src and Sink in one group (mailboxes there).
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t && cd %S/../Driver/Inputs/mailbox
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/plain --static --nest --modulo --compact-links --csf-single-bank --csf-mailbox-builder Src Sink 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=PLAIN
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique --top-module tb -Mdir %t/plain/obj %S/Inputs/tb_reset.sv top.sv %t/plain/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/plain/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/plain/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+1 +stall=0 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/plain/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+2 +stall=40 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=PLAINSIM < %t/plain/foldsim_sim.mlir
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/blk --static --nest --modulo --compact-links --csf-single-bank --csf-mailbox-builder --link-block-depth 2 Src Sink 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=PLAIN
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique --top-module tb -Mdir %t/blk/obj %S/Inputs/tb_reset.sv top.sv %t/blk/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/blk/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/blk/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+3 +stall=0 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/blk/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+4 +stall=40 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=BLKSIM < %t/blk/foldsim_sim.mlir
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/cp --static --nest --modulo --compact-links --csf-single-bank --csf-mailbox-builder --copies Src:2 --link-block-depth 2 Src Sink 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=CP
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique --top-module tb -Mdir %t/cp/obj %S/Inputs/tb_reset.sv top.sv %t/cp/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/cp/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/cp/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+5 +stall=0 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/cp/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+6 +stall=40 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/zl --static --nest --modulo --compact-links --csf-single-bank --csf-mailbox-builder --bubbles --share-links --zero-latency-links --zero-latency-chains Src Sink 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=ZL
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique --top-module tb -DBUBBLES -Mdir %t/zl/obj %S/Inputs/tb_reset.sv top.sv %t/zl/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/zl/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/zl/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+7 +stall=0 +bubble=0 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/zl/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+8 +stall=40 +bubble=30 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/slr --static --nest --modulo --compact-links --csf-single-bank --csf-mailbox-builder --slr-groups --slr-count 2 --slr-assign Src:0,Sink:0,Top_model:1 --link-block-depth 2 Src Sink 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=PLAIN
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique --top-module tb -Mdir %t/slr/obj %S/Inputs/tb_reset.sv top.sv %t/slr/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/slr/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/slr/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+9 +stall=0 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/slr/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+10 +stall=40 | FileCheck %s
# tree-arb: the join levels read two slices each (fan-in 2), with staged,
# shared and zero-latency links around them.
# RUN: cd %S/../Driver/Inputs/tree-arb
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/tz --static --no-drop-dead-inputs --no-staged-link-direct --nest --modulo --compact-links --staged-links --share-links --zero-latency-links --zero-latency-chains --class-at 'sl@*.slice' --class-at 'root@inner:arb' --csf-single-bank --csf-mailbox-builder 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=TZ
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique --top-module tb -Mdir %t/tz/obj %S/Inputs/tb_reset.sv top.sv %t/tz/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/tz/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/tz/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+3 +stall=0 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/tz/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+4 +stall=60 | FileCheck %s
# `--csf-mailbox-hbm`: the mailboxes in HBM, a stream of reader rows each
# (Src -> Sink: two Sink rows of four lanes; Sink -> Src: a stream a lane, its
# Src rows), written byte-masked at the producer's pass, a row landing for
# each reader pass in the stream's landing slots, two sets of read registers
# in turn (no spacing of the reader's passes). Against the controllers'
# model (Inputs/tb_mailbox_hbm.sv: 1 to 60 host cycles, stalls, full, the
# protocol checked), frames of 40 and 24 (min-ii) with bubbles, and with the
# on-chip builder, shared and staged links beside.
# RUN: cd %S/../Driver/Inputs/mailbox
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/h40 --static --nest --modulo --min-ii 40 --compact-links --csf-mailbox-hbm --bubbles Src Sink 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=HBM
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=HBMS < %t/h40/schedule.txt
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=HBMVH < %t/h40/foldsim_sim.vh
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique --top-module tb -I%t/h40 -DVM1 -DVM2 -DVM3 -DVM4 -DBUBBLES -Mdir %t/h40/obj %S/Inputs/tb_mailbox_hbm.sv top.sv %t/h40/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/h40/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/h40/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+1 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/h40/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+2 +stall=30 +lo=1 +hi=20 +full=20 +bubble=20 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/h40/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+4 +lo=1 +hi=60 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/h24 --static --nest --modulo --min-ii 24 --compact-links --share-links --staged-links --csf-single-bank --csf-mailbox-builder --csf-mailbox-hbm --bubbles Src Sink > %t/h24.log 2>&1
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=HBMS < %t/h24/schedule.txt
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique --top-module tb -I%t/h24 -DVM1 -DVM2 -DVM3 -DVM4 -DBUBBLES -Mdir %t/h24/obj %S/Inputs/tb_mailbox_hbm.sv top.sv %t/h24/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/h24/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/h24/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+5 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/h24/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+6 +stall=30 +lo=1 +hi=20 +full=20 +bubble=20 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/h24/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+7 +lo=1 +hi=60 | FileCheck %s
# HBM: II = 40
# HBMS: link streams: 5 streams, 12 links, 80 bits
# HBMS: link stream Src Sink 8 0 32 32 1 8 2 1
# HBMVH: FOLDSIM_VMEM_4_DW 32
# HBMVH-NEXT: FOLDSIM_VMEM_4_MW 4
# PLAIN: csf mailboxes: 2 (1 two banks) of 2 plans, 11 links as lanes (416 producer-entry bits), 2 memories (2 masked), 224 bits
# CP: csf mailboxes: 4 (2 two banks) of 4 plans, 22 links as lanes (416 producer-entry bits), 4 memories (4 masked), 320 bits
# ZL: csf mailboxes: 2 (1 two banks) of 2 plans, 10 links as lanes (320 producer-entry bits), 2 memories (2 masked), 192 bits
# TZ: csf mailboxes: 1 (1 two banks) of 1 plans, 4 links as lanes (108 producer-entry bits), 1 memories (1 masked), 128 bits
# A mailbox: a reader row per Sink, written with a byte mask.
# PLAINSIM: %Src_to_Sink_mbox0_0 = seq.firmem 0, 1, undefined, undefined : <4 x 32, mask 4>
# BLKSIM: %Src_to_Sink_mbox0_0 = seq.firmem 1, 1, old, undefined {{.*}}block{{.*}} : <4 x 32, mask 4>
# CHECK: {{^}}MATCH
# CHECK-NOT: MISMATCH
